        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Sebastien Buisson",
          "email": "sbuisson@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-16 14:54:44.000000000",
          "tz": 120
        },
        "subject": "LU-20972 utils: bound the memory used by parallel find",
        "message": "LU-20972 utils: bound the memory used by parallel find\n\nParallel find queues a work unit for every subdirectory it finds, with\na deep copy of the find_param, and does not limit the number of queued\nunits. The copy is about 75 KB per subdirectory: it is OOM-killed on a\n1.4 GB VM for a directory with 20000 subdirectories, while the serial\ntraversal needs 3 MB.\n\nThese buffers are refilled for every object, so do not copy them\ninto the work units. Each worker thread owns one set, sized as\ncommon_param_init() and xattr_match_info_append() size them, and\nlends it to the work unit it processes, as the serial traversal\nuses a single set. This also fixes a 1-byte heap overflow: the copy\nof xattr_value_buf had XATTR_SIZE_MAX bytes instead of\nXATTR_SIZE_MAX + 1, and find_check_xattrs() writes a '0' after a\nvalue that is not NUL-terminated.\n\nAlso bound the work queue: when FIND_QUEUE_MAX_UNITS work units are\nqueued or being processed, a thread traverses the subdirectory it\nfinds inline, as the serial code does, instead of queuing it. Making\nthe producers wait for room could deadlock, as the producers are the\nworker threads themselves.\n\nA thread that traverses a subdirectory inline keeps open the directory\nit was reading, so its open files grow with the depth it walks inline,\nwhere a worker used to hold about two. To stay within the soft limit\nof open files, parallel_find() derives from it how many levels each\nthread may walk inline. A thread at that depth queues the\nsubdirectory, even if the queue is full.\n\nWith these changes, \"lfs find\" on the 20000 subdirectories peaks at\n7.5 MB, and on a tree of 50000 directories at 7 MB.\n\nAdd sanity test 56Em to exercise this.\n\nFixes: 8f2fb73bc7ff (\"LU-17814 utils: Add deep copy of find_param\")\nSigned-off-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I5bb935a26973c08c5b7f61ebd09352edf6abd338\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
